For ¹³C (spin‑½), equilibrium polarization is

\[
P=\tanh\!\left(\frac{\gamma\hbar B}{2k_BT}\right)\approx \frac{\gamma\hbar B}{2k_BT}
\]

Using \(\gamma_{^{13}C}=10.7084\ \text{MHz/T}\), \(B=20.0\ \text{T}\), \(T=300\ \text{K}\):

\[
\frac{h\nu}{2k_BT}=\frac{\nu}{2(k_BT/h)}
=\frac{(10.7084\times10^6)(20.0)}{2(6.251\times10^{12})}
\approx 1.71\times10^{-5}
\]

So \(P\approx 1.71\times10^{-5}\).

Answer: B
